cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "solar_rhythm: the sound and data processing of The 25th Cycle and Solar Flares, in the browser"
abstract: >-
  Readable, executable translation of the sound and data processing shared by
  the audiovisual works The 25th Cycle (installation) and Solar Flares (live
  performance). The browser page turns the daily sunspot record (SILSO, 1818 to
  today) into a drone, percussion, timbre and form for a Eurorack system, through
  Web MIDI and an Expert Sleepers FH-2. A drone runs through every phase of the solar
  cycle; over it, each phase has its own percussion (Crater, Kraken and the hits
  of a Make Noise Strega), whose number of hits and timbre follow the data, each
  voice on its own loop length. The Max/MSP patches of the installation, which
  also recombine the cycle and drive the image, are not included.
